  "assumptions": [
    "Only the four named active size/powertrain scopes change; all other effective defaults are preserved.",
    "Kick-scooter glider uses a mechanical scooter retail price per kg, divided by the 1.2 reference markup. Transfer to the electric glider is an engineering assumption.",
    "For mopeds and small scooters, subtract the frozen 2025 model non-glider components from a manufacturer price, then divide by the model reference glider mass and markup. This residual is not a measured frame/body production cost.",
    "The unexplained EUR 300 heat-pump charge is excluded from residual calibration but remains in runtime purchase cost pending a separate repair. It must not be absorbed into the glider estimate.",
    "Runtime battery, motor, charger, exhaust-treatment and replacement calculations remain separate. Subsequent changes in their costs must change the purchase total; the residual is never recalculated at runtime.",
    "Reference prices include retail margins and, where specified, VAT. Dividing by reference markup prevents counting that model factor twice; this is not a separation of VAT or factory cost.",
    "Only the Piaggio price has a documented 2025 date. Other displayed prices were retrieved in 2026 and are undated proxies for the 2025 model, without inflation adjustment.",
    "Carry each slope and zero intercept unchanged across 2000-2050 to avoid introducing a 2025 discontinuity. This is a constant scenario assumption, not a reconstruction of historical or forecast nominal prices. Legacy components retain mixed price bases.",
    "Retain each native year original relative triangular slope bounds. These are engineering uncertainty, not statistical confidence intervals from the manufacturer observations."
  ],
  "known_limits": [
    "Complete purchase totals remain sensitive to inherited component assumptions, notably heat pumps and chargers; fix those separately without refitting away their effects.",
    "Source vehicles have different masses, capacities, national markets and equipment from the generic models. Matching a calibration anchor is not independent validation.",
    "Human bicycle cost defaults remain incomplete; other classes and full ownership-cost categories remain outside this repair."
  ],
